@startuml context-web
' SplitSmart - System context and runtime containers, Alternative A (web, recommended)
' Source of truth: architecture.md sections 2.2, 3.4, 7.1. Technologies marked <<proposal>> are not customer requirements.
title SplitSmart - Context & Containers (Alternative A: Web)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Account holder\n(member / manager / approver)" as User

node "User device" {
  component "Web browser\n(SPA client)" as Browser
}

node "Application host <<proposal>>" {
  component "splitsmart-web\nSpring Boot JAR (Java 21)\nREST API /api/v1 + static SPA assets" as App
}

database "PostgreSQL <<proposal>>\naccounts, groups, expenses,\nallocations, decisions, payments,\nnotifications" as DB
folder "Receipt storage <<proposal>>\n(private volume or object store)" as Files
cloud "SMTP relay <<proposal>>\n(password-reset email only)" as SMTP

User --> Browser : uses
Browser --> App : HTTPS JSON\n(session cookie + CSRF token)
App --> DB : JDBC / JPA\n(transactions, row locks)
App --> Files : read/write receipt images
App --> SMTP : send reset links
SMTP ..> User : email

note right of App
  In-app notifications are stored in the DB;
  the browser polls /me/notifications/unread-count.
  Other channels: Open Question 3.
end note
@enduml
